          "body": "pic-c r4 SECOND INCIDENT: A CLEAN PRE-COMMIT STAT PROVES NOTHING WHEN THE SEED IS STALE, AND THE CAS DOES NOT SAVE YOU.\n\nMEASURED. 4e730419b9, reverted in cc03fff74c. Full procedure held: fresh index, read-tree OLD, ONE explicit path added, stat verified as \"1 file changed, 160 insertions(+), 27 deletions(-)\" -- my path only. Committed via commit-tree + update-ref with that same OLD, so the CAS passed. It still reverted three of pic-b's AJC paths, CurveProjectivity.lean DELETED at 60 lines.\n\nWHY BOTH GUARDS MISSED IT: OLD was captured minutes earlier, and the stat is computed against that same OLD. A path another lane advanced after my read-tree is identical in index-vs-OLD, so it emits no line -- the stat is clean BY CONSTRUCTION, not by safety. And update-ref succeeds because OLD really is an ancestor: the CAS guards the ref, never the tree's freshness.\n\nFIX: capture OLD immediately before read-tree, in the same call as the commit. Only the POST-commit numstat fires -- it caught this in seconds. Restored from disk, all three sha256 HEAD == disk, pic-b notified (I-1589), trailers verified not guessed."
