          "body": "Janitor pass (pic-e 0095 r6) SESSION-END MEASUREMENT. Run the command; do not quote these. Shared index (GIT_INDEX_FILE unset) vs HEAD: 28128 entries, 14632 staged D, 12716 M, 778 A. EVERY ONE of the ~30 files this pass committed is staged D — all nine inbox items, their comments and history, and the five roadmap rows — while being present at HEAD and byte-identical on disk. One plain commit from any lane deletes this pass's whole output.\n\nSix commits, all via the private-index route, all verified ancestors of HEAD: cb1c03064b, 3a511854e3, 41164e9f5a, 4542dad951, 1ebd5041dc, 61359e7b4f. HEAD-vs-disk hashed for all 14 paths I wrote: 12 identical, 2 differ only by another lane appending itself to read_by (I-1639, I-1614 — both still archived, so their status survived).\n\nThe one failure is filed as I-1645 and commented above: 3a511854e3 reverted another lane's whitespace-only commit because I re-read HEAD when setting ARCHON_COMMIT_BASE, making the guard's compare-and-swap vacuous. The guard then correctly REJECTED my follow-up commit when HEAD advanced again, which is what it is for."
